results/analysis/t_b8_oversub_5070ti/telemetry_n10_verify/*.bin
results/analysis/t_b8_oversub_5070ti/telemetry_depth0_verify/*.bin

# Gate B9: oversubscription mechanism block -- raw per-run telemetry rings,
# oracle trace files, and nsys reports (large, reconstructible by rerunning
# the tests/t_b9_*.sh harnesses -- the CSVs (task*_times.csv,
# task*_aggregate_comparison.csv, task*_run_summary.csv) and
# GATE_B9_OVERSUB_MECHANISM.md / GATE_B9_TASK2_REBUILD.md carry the numbers
# that matter, same convention as every telemetry/*.bin pattern above)
results/analysis/gate_b9_oversub_mechanism/telemetry_*/
results/analysis/gate_b9_oversub_mechanism/task1_nsys_reports/
results/analysis/gate_b9_oversub_mechanism/task1_smi_polls/
results/analysis/gate_b9_oversub_mechanism/*.bin

# Gate B10: augmentation block (C0-vs-C4) -- same convention as Gate B9
# above: raw per-run telemetry (watchdog markers, wall-clock scratch files),
# oracle trace .bin files, and the launcher's own stdout log are all
# reconstructible by rerunning tests/t_b10_c0_vs_c4.sh. The CSVs
# (t_b10_c0_vs_c4_times.csv, t_b10_aggregate_comparison.csv,
# t_b10_atomics_summary.csv), the analysis script, and
# GATE_B10_AUGMENTATION.md carry the numbers that matter.
results/analysis/gate_b10_augmentation/telemetry_b10/
results/analysis/gate_b10_augmentation/*.bin
results/analysis/gate_b10_augmentation/run.log

# Gate B10 Task C+D: replication (iters=20) + crossover fill (iters=8,12,16)
# -- same convention as Gate B10 above, reconstructible by rerunning
# tests/t_b10c_replication_crossover.sh.
results/analysis/gate_b10_replication/telemetry_b10c/
results/analysis/gate_b10_replication/*.bin
results/analysis/gate_b10_replication/run.log
